  <script type="application/json" data-target="react-app.embeddedData">{"payload":{"preloaded_records":{},"structured_data":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","headline":"Timing of cloning for the `\u003cselectedoption\u003e` element","articleBody":"### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe `\u003cselectedoption\u003e` element is discussed more generally here, and this issue is for a topic which has been split out: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10242\r\n\r\nWhen the author modifies content inside an `\u003coption\u003e` element, we will clone the contents of that `\u003coption\u003e` into the `\u003cselectedoption\u003e`, but the timing at which we do this cloning has not yet been decided.\r\n\r\nThe timing will be web observable. For example, if the author modifies an option and then tries to query the layout of `\u003cselectedoption\u003e`, they will have to wait until the cloning happens.\r\n\r\nSome possible options for cloning timing are:\r\n1. Synchronously\r\n2. Microtask timing\r\n3. CustomElements reaction timing\r\n4. Something slower?\r\n\r\nI think that we should do microtask timing because I am planning on using a MutationObserver internally to implement this, and MutationObserver already uses microtask timing: https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#queue-a-mutation-observer-compound-microtask\r\n\r\nIf we diverge from microtask timing, we would have to make a special kind of mutationobserver that does different timing, right?\r\n\r\n@emilio @smaug---- ","author":{"url":"https://github.com/josepharhar","@type":"Person","name":"josepharhar"},"datePublished":"2024-07-25T17:56:27.000Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"https://schema.org/CommentAction","userInteractionCount":65},"url":"https://github.com/10520/html/issues/10520"},"best_match_sort_enabled":false,"issue_search_type":"ISSUE_HYBRID","preloadedQueries":[{"queryId":"3df89a31f92b42d0a56f3714504d7fc1","queryName":"IssueViewerViewQuery","variables":{"count":15,"number":10520,"owner":"whatwg","repo":"html"},"result":{"data":{"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxMTk2OTUwNw==","isOwnerEnterpriseManaged":false,"owner":{"__typename":"Organization","userNameDisplayConfiguration":"HANDLE","id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjIyMjYzMzY="},"issue":{"id":"I_kwDOALaj486Q4Qx2","number":10520,"viewerCanUpdateMetadata":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxMTk2OTUwNw==","databaseId":11969507,"name":"html","isArchived":false,"nameWithOwner":"whatwg/html","viewerCanInteract":false,"viewerInteractionLimitReasonHTML":"","slashCommandsEnabled":false,"visibility":"PUBLIC","viewerCanPush":false,"owner":{"__typename":"Organization","login":"whatwg","id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjIyMjYzMzY=","url":"https://github.com/whatwg","databaseId":2226336,"issueFieldsEnabled":true,"issueFields":{"totalCount":0},"pinnedIssueFields":{"nodes":[]}},"isPrivate":false,"isWritable":true,"isOwnerEnterpriseManaged":false,"viewerCanPinIssues":false,"isCopilotAgentEnabled":null,"issueTypes":{"edges":[{"node":{"id":"IT_kwDOACH4oM4AA-yk"}},{"node":{"id":"IT_kwDOACH4oM4AA-ym"}},{"node":{"id":"IT_kwDOACH4oM4AA-yp"}}]},"pinnedIssues":{"totalCount":0},"viewerIssueCreationPermissions":{"triageable":false}},"updatedAt":"2025-07-22T03:42:00Z","titleHTML":"Timing of cloning for the \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;selectedoption\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e element","url":"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10520","viewerCanUpdateNext":false,"issueType":null,"duplicateOf":null,"linkedPullRequests":{"nodes":[{"repository":{"name":"html","nameWithOwner":"whatwg/html","owner":{"__typename":"Organization","login":"whatwg","id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjIyMjYzMzY="},"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxMTk2OTUwNw=="},"url":"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10548","number":10548,"state":"MERGED","isDraft":false,"id":"PR_kwDOALaj4853dGi-"}]},"agentAssignments":[],"closedByPullRequestsReferences":{"nodes":[{"id":"PR_kwDOALaj485788s9","number":10633,"url":"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10633","state":"CLOSED","databaseId":2079574845},{"id":"PR_kwDOALaj4853dGi-","number":10548,"url":"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10548","state":"MERGED","databaseId":2004117694}]},"labels":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"MQ"},"edges":[{"node":{"id":"LA_kwDOALaj488AAAABzBmV7g","color":"009800","name":"topic: select","nameHTML":"topic: select","description":"The \u003cselect\u003e element","url":"https://github.com/whatwg/html/labels/topic%3A%20select"}}]},"milestone":null,"assignedActors":{"nodes":[]},"locked":false,"viewerCanComment":false,"databaseId":2430667894,"state":"CLOSED","stateReason":"COMPLETED","title":"Timing of cloning for the `\u003cselectedoption\u003e` element","createdAt":"2024-07-25T17:56:27Z","viewerDidAuthor":false,"author":{"avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7681467?u=975aa36c2bf890f0c3f43db7a9d653fd4ad5a5f2\u0026v=4","login":"josepharhar","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2ODE0Njc=","profileUrl":"https://github.com/josepharhar","name":"Joey Arhar","__typename":"User"},"body":"### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe `\u003cselectedoption\u003e` element is discussed more generally here, and this issue is for a topic which has been split out: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10242\r\n\r\nWhen the author modifies content inside an `\u003coption\u003e` element, we will clone the contents of that `\u003coption\u003e` into the `\u003cselectedoption\u003e`, but the timing at which we do this cloning has not yet been decided.\r\n\r\nThe timing will be web observable. For example, if the author modifies an option and then tries to query the layout of `\u003cselectedoption\u003e`, they will have to wait until the cloning happens.\r\n\r\nSome possible options for cloning timing are:\r\n1. Synchronously\r\n2. Microtask timing\r\n3. CustomElements reaction timing\r\n4. Something slower?\r\n\r\nI think that we should do microtask timing because I am planning on using a MutationObserver internally to implement this, and MutationObserver already uses microtask timing: https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#queue-a-mutation-observer-compound-microtask\r\n\r\nIf we diverge from microtask timing, we would have to make a special kind of mutationobserver that does different timing, right?\r\n\r\n@emilio @smaug---- ","bodyHTML":"\u003ch3 dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhat is the issue with the HTML Standard?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u0026lt;selectedoption\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e element is discussed more generally here, and this issue is for a topic which has been split out: \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2257699982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10242\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10242/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10242\"\u003ew3c/csswg-drafts#10242\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhen the author modifies content inside an \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u0026lt;option\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e element, we will clone the contents of that \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u0026lt;option\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e into the \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u0026lt;selectedoption\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e, but the timing at which we do this cloning has not yet been decided.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe timing will be web observable. For example, if the author modifies an option and then tries to query the layout of \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u0026lt;selectedoption\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e, they will have to wait until the cloning happens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eSome possible options for cloning timing are:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSynchronously\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMicrotask timing\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCustomElements reaction timing\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSomething slower?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI think that we should do microtask timing because I am planning on using a MutationObserver internally to implement this, and MutationObserver already uses microtask timing: \u003ca href=\"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#queue-a-mutation-observer-compound-microtask\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#queue-a-mutation-observer-compound-microtask\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf we diverge from microtask timing, we would have to make a special kind of mutationobserver that does different timing, right?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/emilio/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/emilio\"\u003e@emilio\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/smaug----/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/smaug----\"\u003e@smaug----\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"650894561463488b30469bfa7623c53953dcc7af5d63e7a529d596f35b73f831","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"THUMBS_DOWN","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"LAUGH","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HOORAY","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"CONFUSED","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"HEART","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes